Because i was actually making my code to just accept only the keyword or topic-name and just give me the answer 
using this code :
def search ( user_input ):
    for item in data:
        if data["topic"].lower() == user_input.lower() :
            return data["content"]
        else:
            return "Not available." 

what i learnt today 

Instead of using "==" I should had used the keyword "in"
this keyword is a membership operator keyword 
it searches through the string the user will provide if the user types any topic (That exist in my json file) in the strings the user provide it detects it and return the content or answer to that particular topic-name.

And the ".lower()" help the "in" keeyword to detect either upper or lower cased topic-name

          